`),LV=["**When to travel India**","","• **October – March** — the mainstream window. Pleasant everywhere, best in the north and the desert.","• **April – June** — the Himalaya opens up, and it is the best time for tigers in the reserves.","• **June – September** — the monsoon. Kerala, Goa and Konkan turn green and dramatic; the plains clear of heat.","• **November – February** — the festivals: Diwali, Durga Puja, Hornbill, Pushkar, Rann Utsav.","","Tell me the state and I will narrow it down."].join(`
`),IV=["**A short tour of Indian food**","","• **North** — tandoori breads, dal makhani, Mughlai kebabs and chole bhature","• **South** — dosa, sambar, Malabar biryani, Chettinad spice and filter coffee","• **East** — mustard-fish, sweets such as rosogolla and kheer, and milk sweets","• **West** — Gujarati thali, dhokla, laal maas, Goan vindaloo and Portuguese plates","• **North East** — smoked pork, bamboo shoot, axone and sticky rice","","Name a state and I will send you its five signature dishes."].join(`
`),OV=["**The festivals that move the country**","","• **Durga Puja** (West Bengal, September) — five nights of pandals","• **Onam** (Kerala, August) — flower carpets and a twenty-course sadya","• **Diwali** (all India, October) — lamps, sweets and family","• **Holi** (north India, March) — the festival of colour","• **Hornbill** (Nagaland, December) — ten days of state dance","• **Pushkar Fair** (Rajasthan, October) — camels, crafts and the desert","• **Baisakhi** (Punjab, April) — harvest, kite-flying and the Khalsa","• **Chhath Puja** (Bihar, November) — four days of dawn and dusk offerings","","Ask me “festivals in Kerala” for the local calendar."].join(`
`),BV=["**A realistic budget**","","• **Backpacker** ₹1,500 – ₹2,500 a day (hostels, trains, street food)","• **Comfort** ₹4,000 – ₹7,000 a day (budget hotels, AC trains, good food)","• **Premium** ₹9,000+ a day (heritage stays, private cars, fine dining)","","**Cost-saving moves** — travel by night train, eat where the locals eat, and book heritage properties directly; many state tourism sites offer better rates than OTAs.","","The curated routes on this page carry per-person estimates — ask me for any of them."].join(`
